  "question": {
    "text": "A conducting square frame of side <math> <mtext>a</mtext> </math> and a long straight wire carrying current <math> <mtext>I</mtext> </math> are located in the same plane as shown in the figure. The frame moves to the right with a constant velocity <math> <mtext>V</mtext></math>. The e.m.f induced in the frame (when the centre of the frame is at a distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> from the wire) will be proportional to :<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0042_fcce1abda084.jpg\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>",
